.TH CMIX 1 "September 2026" "cmix 21" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmix \- Extreme lossless data compression program using context mixing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmix
.RB [ \-c | \-d | \-t | \-n | \-s ]
.RI [ dictionary ]
.I input
.RI [ output ]
.br
.B cmix
.RB [ \-c | \-d ]
<
.I input
>
.I output
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmix
is a lossless data compression program written by Byron Knoll that achieves state-of-the-art compression ratios using an ensemble of context models (PPM, PAQ8, indirect hashes, interval models) combined via a recurrent LSTM neural network.
.PP
.B cmix
prioritizes compression ratio above all else. It is computationally demanding and requires substantial CPU and RAM resources. A machine with at least 32 GB of RAM is strongly recommended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Compress
.I input
file into
.IR output .
If no file arguments are given and standard input is redirected, reads from stdin and writes to stdout.
.TP
.B \-d
Decompress
.I input
archive into
.IR output .
If no file arguments are given and standard input is redirected, reads from stdin and writes to stdout.
.TP
.B \-t
Test the integrity of
.IR archive .
Decompresses into memory/temporary space and verifies validity without modifying destination files.
.TP
.B \-n
Compress without preprocessing transformations.
.TP
.B \-s
Run only the preprocessing step without context mixing.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display command usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-V, \-\-version
Display program version and exit.
.SH TAR INTEGRATION
.B cmix
can be used with GNU
.BR tar (1)
as a compression filter:
.PP
.RS
tar \-\-use-compress-program=cmix \-cf archive.tar.cmix file1 file2
.br
tar \-\-use-compress-program="cmix \-d" \-xf archive.tar.cmix
.RE
